# {{ name }} — Register Features & Architecture Specification

**Project:** {{ name }}  
**Register Data Width:** {{ reg_width }}-bit ({{ reg_width_bytes }} bytes per word)  
**Description:** {{ description }}

---

## 1. Architectural Overview & Bus Interface

This document specifies the architectural features, access semantics, hardware precedence rules, and sideband signaling for all registers implemented in **{{ name }}**.

- **Bus Data Width:** `{{ reg_width }}` bits. Accesses are aligned to `{{ reg_width_bytes }}`-byte word boundaries.
{% if existsIn(features, "has_byte_strobes") and features.has_byte_strobes %}
- **Byte Write Strobing:** Granular byte-write strobe signals (`wstrb`) enable partial-word updates without altering neighboring bytes.
{% endif %}
{% if existsIn(features, "has_hw_precedence") and features.has_hw_precedence %}
- **Hardware Precedence:** In case of simultaneous hardware and software writes to the same bitfield, hardware writes take strict precedence over software bus writes to guarantee hardware event integrity.
{% endif %}
{% if existsIn(features, "has_address_gaps") and features.has_address_gaps %}
- **Sparse Addressing:** Memory map contains non-contiguous register offsets with decoded gap alignment.
{% endif %}

---

## 2. Register Access Policies Implemented

The register blocks in this specification implement the following IEEE 1800.2 access policies ({{ features.access_policies_str }}):

| Access Policy | Access Type | Software Behavior | Hardware Behavior | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
{% if existsIn(features, "has_rw") and features.has_rw %}| `RW` | Read / Write | Read returns current value; Write updates field. | Internal state output. | Standard read/write control and configuration field. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_ro") and features.has_ro %}| `RO` | Read-Only | Read returns current value; Write is ignored. | Hardware updates or drives state. | Status indicators, sensor readings, and hardware counters. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_wo") and features.has_wo %}| `WO` | Write-Only | Read returns 0; Write updates field. | Internal state output. | Trigger commands and security-sensitive keys. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_w1c") and features.has_w1c %}| `W1C` | Write-1-to-Clear | Read returns current value; Write `1` clears bit to `0`, write `0` has no effect. | Hardware sets bit on event. | Interrupt request (IRQ) pending flags and sticky event latches. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_w1s") and features.has_w1s %}| `W1S` | Write-1-to-Set | Read returns current value; Write `1` sets bit to `1`, write `0` has no effect. | Hardware clears bit. | Software trigger flags and manual event asserting. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_w1t") and features.has_w1t %}| `W1T` | Write-1-to-Toggle | Read returns current value; Write `1` inverts bit, write `0` has no effect. | Internal state output. | Diagnostic test toggles and periodic pin inversion. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_w0c") and features.has_w0c %}| `W0C` | Write-0-to-Clear | Read returns current value; Write `0` clears bit to `0`, write `1` has no effect. | Hardware sets bit. | Active-low interrupt clear flags. |
{% endif %}{% if existsIn(features, "has_rc") and features.has_rc %}| `RC` | Read-to-Clear | Read returns current value and clears bit to `0`; Write is ignored. | Hardware increments or sets. | Sticky event counters and auto-acknowledging interrupts. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_rs %}| `RS` | Read-to-Set | Read returns current value and sets bit to `1`; Write is ignored. | Hardware clears bit. | Semaphore and token acquisition flags. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_wc %}| `WC` | Write-Clear | Software write clears field to 0; Read returns current value. | Hardware sets or updates. | Software command clear register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_ws %}| `WS` | Write-Set | Software write sets all bits to 1; Read returns current value. | Hardware clears or updates. | Software command set register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_w1src %}| `W1SRC` | Write-1-Set-Read-Clear | Write `1` sets field, read clears field to 0. | Internal hardware logic. | Dual-action handshake register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_w1crs %}| `W1CRS` | Write-1-Clear-Read-Set | Write `1` clears field, read sets field to 1. | Internal hardware logic. | Inverted handshake register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_w0src %}| `W0SRC` | Write-0-Set-Read-Clear | Write `0` sets field, read clears field to 0. | Internal hardware logic. | Active-low handshake register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_w0crs %}| `W0CRS` | Write-0-Clear-Read-Set | Write `0` clears field, read sets field to 1. | Internal hardware logic. | Active-low inverted handshake. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_woc %}| `WOC` | Write-Only-Clear | Write clears field to 0; Read returns 0. | Internal hardware logic. | Blind clear command register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_wos %}| `WOS` | Write-Only-Set | Write sets field to 1; Read returns 0. | Internal hardware logic. | Blind set command register. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_w1 %}| `W1` | Write-Once | First write after reset updates field; subsequent writes are ignored. | Read by hardware. | Boot-time lock and security configuration registers. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_wo1 %}| `WO1` | Write-Once-Only | Write-only field that can only be written once after reset; read returns 0. | Read by hardware. | Write-once security keys and authorization words. |
{% endif %}{% if features.has_noaccess %}| `NOACCESS` | No Access | Software cannot read or write (access returns bus error or zeros). | Internal hardware use. | Reserved or security-isolated bitfields. |
{% endif %}

