## 4. Hardware Sideband & Strobe Signaling

For each register field with active hardware interaction:

{% if existsIn(features, "has_hw_writable") and features.has_hw_writable %}
- **Hardware Write Signals (`hw_<reg>_<fld>_i`, `hw_<reg>_<fld>_we_i`)**: When `hw_we` is asserted, hardware updates the field with `hw_i` on the rising clock edge, overriding any pending software write.
{% endif %}
{% if existsIn(features, "has_hw_readable") and features.has_hw_readable %}
- **Hardware Value Signals (`hw_<reg>_<fld>_o`)**: Continuously driven with the current registered field state for direct peripheral logic consumption.
{% endif %}
- **Software Read Strobe (`sw_<reg>_<fld>_rd_strobe_o`)**: Active-high 1-cycle pulse generated whenever software executes a successful bus read targeting this register.
- **Software Write Strobe (`sw_<reg>_<fld>_wr_strobe_o`)**: Active-high 1-cycle pulse generated whenever software executes a bus write targeting this register.
